  "Number": 12,
  "Question": "What is the value of\n\n\\[\\frac{1 - \\frac{1}{3}}{1 - \\frac{1}{2}}?\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{1}{3}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac{2}{3}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{3}{4}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{3}{2}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{4}{3}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "First do the subtraction above and below the main fraction bar:\n\\[\n1-\\frac13=\\frac33-\\frac13=\\frac23,\n\\qquad\n1-\\frac12=\\frac22-\\frac12=\\frac12.\n\\]\nThe denominator is \\(\\frac12\\), which is nonzero. Dividing by \\(\\frac12\\) means multiplying by its reciprocal, \\(2\\), so\n\\[\n\\frac{1-\\frac13}{1-\\frac12}\n=\\frac23\\div\\frac12\n=\\frac23\\times2\n=\\frac43.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\frac43\\), choice E.",
